# Huawei SFS Turbo Quota Notes

- Never commit or document Huawei Cloud AK/SK values. Use local `env.sh` only; it is git-ignored and should remain `chmod 600`.
- In this repo, `new_cluster.yaml` currently has no StorageClass. The Huawei SFS Turbo classes are in `new_cluster_prod.yaml`.
- `managed-nfs-storage-2..5` use `nfs.csi.k8s.io` with servers like `<share_id>.sfsturbo.internal` and `share: /`; historical PVs also reference `managed-nfs-storage-1`.
- Kubernetes PVC `requests.storage` only becomes PV metadata for these SFS Turbo mounts. It does not enforce quota by itself; Pod `df` can show the whole ~100T filesystem.
- For a dynamically provisioned PVC, read the PV's `spec.csi.volumeAttributes.server` and `subdir`. The SFSTurbo directory quota API should target `share_id=<server prefix>` and `path=/<subdir>`.
- Verify quota by writing past the configured capacity from a test Pod and expecting `No space left on device`/EDQUOT, then clean up the test Pod/PVC.
